\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She sat very straight in a winged chair richly covered with petit point, her elicate claw-like hands lay lightly folded on her silken lap, and her eyes\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8230\'85 the eyes of an old lady eagle who has looked long and perhaps not too discreetly on the sun.. Showed a slight grayish glaze. Which meat that the read had lasted nearly its appointed two hours and the attention of the Marchesa was teetering.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93He\u8217\'92s strong meat,\u8221\'94 said the Marchesa, wagging gray curls above a  withered throat, perennially swathed in a black velvet band\u8230\'85 \u8220\'93Strong meat, Swinburne, \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0  too strong for your type, Miss wayne. Just as well let him be. Read-ah, WOrdsworth\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 if you must!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 change idiot to \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I couldn\u8217\'92t agree more\u8221\'94.}
